---
// 07 · Seeds — What's Growing. Copy from the former /seeds page; the
// seeds-and-sprout scene is ported from the prototype, recolored (ochre
// seeds in karkadeh soil, a river-green sprout). The three asks float over
// the art as seed chips opening the shared popover, and stand as cards below.
---

<section id="seeds" class="journey" data-number="07" aria-labelledby="seeds-title">
  <div class="art reveal">
    <div class="seeds-scene">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 480 450" role="img" aria-label="Seeds and a new sprout emerging from rich soil">
        <defs>
          <radialGradient id="seed-glow" cx="0.5" cy="0.5" r="0.5">
            <stop offset="0" style="stop-color: var(--ochre-light)" stop-opacity="0.35" />
            <stop offset="1" style="stop-color: var(--ochre)" stop-opacity="0" />
          </radialGradient>
          <linearGradient id="sprout-grad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0" style="stop-color: var(--river-light)" />
            <stop offset="1" style="stop-color: var(--river-deep)" />
          </linearGradient>
        </defs>

        <path d="M20 370 Q240 320 460 370 L460 450 L20 450Z" style="fill: var(--karkadeh)" />
        <path class="draw" d="M35 376 Q240 332 445 376" fill="none" style="stroke: var(--ochre)" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <path d="M60 390 Q240 355 420 390" fill="none" style="stroke: var(--karkadeh-deep)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.4" />

        <g class="soil-particle" style="fill: var(--ochre)" opacity="0.35">
          <circle cx="100" cy="400" r="3" /><circle cx="350" cy="410" r="2.5" /><circle cx="220" cy="420" r="2" />
        </g>
        <g class="soil-particle sp2" style="fill: var(--ochre)" opacity="0.3">
          <circle cx="280" cy="395" r="2" /><circle cx="150" cy="415" r="3" /><circle cx="380" cy="405" r="2.5" />
        </g>

        <g class="grow g1" style="transform-origin: 155px 340px">
          <ellipse cx="155" cy="340" rx="14" ry="20" style="fill: var(--ochre)" transform="rotate(-18 155 340)" />
          <ellipse cx="155" cy="340" rx="10" ry="16" style="fill: var(--ochre-light)" transform="rotate(-18 155 340)" opacity="0.6" />
          <circle cx="155" cy="340" r="30" fill="url(#seed-glow)" opacity="0.5" />
        </g>
        <g class="grow g2" style="transform-origin: 330px 350px">
          <ellipse cx="330" cy="350" rx="12" ry="18" style="fill: var(--river-pale)" transform="rotate(16 330 350)" />
          <ellipse cx="330" cy="350" rx="8" ry="14" style="fill: var(--river-light)" transform="rotate(16 330 350)" opacity="0.5" />
          <circle cx="330" cy="350" r="25" fill="url(#seed-glow)" opacity="0.3" />
        </g>

        <g class="sprout-grow">
          <path d="M240 368 C238 318 242 274 254 228" fill="none" style="stroke: var(--river-deep)" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round" />
          <path d="M254 248 C280 228 306 226 322 232 C310 256 280 264 254 248 Z" fill="url(#sprout-grad)" />
          <path d="M252 276 C228 260 204 260 190 268 C204 288 232 292 252 276 Z" style="fill: var(--river-light)" />
          <path d="M254 248 C280 228 306 226 322 232" fill="none" style="stroke: var(--river-deep)" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.5" />
          <path d="M252 276 C228 260 204 260 190 268" fill="none" style="stroke: var(--river-deep)" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.5" />

          <g style="fill: var(--river-light)" opacity="0.7">
            <path class="realistic-leaf" d="M290 235 C295 231 304 232 306 237 C302 242 295 241 290 237Z" />
            <path class="realistic-leaf rl2" d="M220 268 C225 264 234 265 236 270 C232 275 225 274 220 270Z" />
          </g>
        </g>

        <g fill="none" style="stroke: var(--river)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.7">
          <path d="M120 380 l-4-10 M126 382 l3-12" />
          <path d="M380 378 l-4-10 M386 380 l3-12" />
        </g>
      </svg>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="chip chip-float seed-chip sc1"
        data-popover-title="Space"
        data-popover-body="Free or low-cost venues where gatherings can root — a room, a yard, a hall that sits empty on weekday evenings. Space is the difference between a plan and a gathering."
        data-popover-link="#contact"
        data-popover-link-text="Offer space →"
      >Space</button>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="chip chip-float seed-chip d2 sc2"
        data-popover-title="Funding"
        data-popover-body="Funding that trusts the people doing the work: multi-year, lightly restricted, sized to the work rather than to a funder's calendar. The Dish With One Spoon, practised at the level of budgets."
        data-popover-link="#contact"
        data-popover-link-text="Talk funding →"
      >Funding</button>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="chip chip-float seed-chip d3 sc3"
        data-popover-title="Capacity"
        data-popover-body="Legal, financial, and administrative strength lent from organizations that have it — for example, a legal or financial team's time toward incorporation. Expertise shared is capacity built."
        data-popover-link="#contact"
        data-popover-link-text="Lend capacity →"
      >Capacity</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="copy">
    <p class="tag reveal">07 · Seeds</p>
    <h2 class="reveal" data-d="1" id="seeds-title">What's growing.</h2>
    <p class="reveal" data-d="2">
      Every gathering Pamoja has grown came from seed: a yard offered, a
      grant trusted, a partner's time lent. This page names what the next
      season needs — and what an investment in a shared community actually
      looks like.
    </p>
    <p class="reveal" data-d="3">
      This is not a donation request. It is an invitation to invest in a
      community you belong to — to put something into the shared dish that
      the whole city eats from.
    </p>
    <a class="cta reveal" data-d="4" href="#contact">Plant something with us →</a>
  </div>

  <div class="ask" style="grid-column: 1 / -1" aria-labelledby="ask-heading">
    <h3 class="reveal" id="ask-heading">The ask.</h3>
    <div class="ask-grid">
      <article class="card ask-card reveal" data-d="1">
        <h4>Space</h4>
        <p>
          Free or low-cost venues where gatherings can root — a room, a yard,
          a hall that sits empty on weekday evenings. Space is the difference
          between a plan and a gathering.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card ask-card reveal" data-d="2">
        <h4>Flexible, multi-year, trust-based funding</h4>
        <p>
          Funding that trusts the people doing the work: multi-year, lightly
          restricted, sized to the work rather than to a funder's calendar.
          The Dish With One Spoon, practised at the level of budgets.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card ask-card reveal" data-d="3">
        <h4>Institutional capacity</h4>
        <p>
          Legal, financial, and administrative strength lent from
          organizations that have it — for example, a legal or financial
          team's time toward incorporation. Expertise shared is capacity
          built.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="examples" style="grid-column: 1 / -1" aria-labelledby="examples-heading">
    <h3 class="reveal" id="examples-heading">What a successful partnership looks like.</h3>
    <ul class="example-list">
      <li class="reveal" data-d="1">
        <strong>Co-hosting a community meal</strong> — your organization's
        people cooking and eating alongside the community's, as guests and
        co-hosts, not sponsors at a distance.
      </li>
      <li class="reveal" data-d="2">
        <strong>Lending a professional team's time toward incorporation</strong> —
        a legal or financial team's hours, given as capacity the collective
        keeps.
      </li>
      <li class="reveal" data-d="3">
        <strong>Sharing unused space</strong> — a venue that stands empty
        becoming common ground for a season or longer.
      </li>
      <li class="reveal" data-d="4">
        <strong>Helping with a crowdfunding campaign</strong> — reach,
        matching, and credibility lent to a campaign the community runs.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="closing-line reveal" style="grid-column: 1 / -1">
    If you have space, funding, capacity, or something we haven't thought to
    ask for — the first step is the same as always:
    <a href="#contact">a conversation</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .seeds-scene {
    position: relative;
    width: min(480px, 84vw);
  }
  .seed-chip {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.85rem;
  }
  .sc1 { left: 24%; top: 66%; }
  .sc2 { right: 22%; top: 70%; }
  .sc3 { left: 42%; top: 38%; }

  .ask h3,
  .examples h3 {
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.5vw, 2.4rem);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .ask-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(280px, 100%), 1fr));
  }
  .ask-card {
    border-top: 4px solid var(--river);
  }
  .ask-card h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--night);
  }
  .ask-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .example-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: var(--max-prose);
  }
  .example-list li {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--cream);
    border-radius: 10px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--ochre);
  }

  .closing-line {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    max-width: var(--max-prose);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
